---
// src/pages/human-ai-interaction.astro
import SectionedPageLayout from '../layouts/SectionedPageLayout.astro';
---

<SectionedPageLayout title="Supervising AI User Study">
  <section
    id="problem"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="problem-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="problem-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Live captioning is very cognitively demanding-- self-reported measures found captioning to be more stressful than
        surgery
      </p>
      <p>
        Automatic Speech Recognition has already replaced captioners in online meetings and post-production events
      </p>
      <p>Broadcasting agencies and governments are not prepared for this inevitable shift</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <video
          src="/videos/live_cc_issues.mp4"
          controls
          class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto"
          aria-label="Problem diagram video"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          Your browser does not support the video tag.
        </video>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Live captioning is intense-- can you spot the multiple mistakes made by professional captioners?
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="methods"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="methods-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="methods-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Methods</h2>
      <p>
        Applied knowledge from psychology, cognitive science, computer science and industrial engineering to conduct a
        study where captioners supervised AI to write captions rather than working alone
      </p>
      <p>
        Mixed-methods approach with 21 captioners using NASA-TLX, System Usability Scale, Nielsen-Norman Satisfaction
        Scale, Trust in Automation Scale and qualitative interviews
      </p>
      <p>Time-series-- 3 sessions spaced 24 hours apart to allow for learning</p>
      <p>Controlled environment and pre-screened for familiarity</p>
      <p>Two independent groups: Novices and Experts-- controlled for skill level</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/methods.png" alt="Research Methods" class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Used a cross-disciplinary approach to develop measurements for 14 constructs in the Human Autonomy System
          Oversight model (which until now was theoretical).
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="findings"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="findings-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="findings-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Findings</h2>
      <p>Mitigating fear is about expectation management</p>
      <p>Captioners desire more control over AI</p>
      <p>AI reduced physical and mental workload over just 3 sessions spaced 24 hours apart</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/findings.png" alt="Findings" class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Saw a statistically significant reduction in mental workload, which led me to test and discover relationships
          not present in the original model.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="recommendations"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="recommendations-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="recommendations-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Recommendations</h2>
      <p>Human benefit from control over AI</p>
      <p>Even if AI can automate the job, manual control should be relegated</p>
      <p>Scheduling is one recommended solution</p>
      <p>Another is interface based (see Design Mock-up from the side menu)</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/loa.png" alt="Recommendations" class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          Based on rigorous analysis, I suggested a model where control and automation is adaptive to user needs. This
          has far-reaching implications for human use over AI.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="impact"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="impact-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="impact-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Impact</h2>
      <p>Led the only study on captioners supervising AI in the world</p>
      <p>Discovered new relationships between Human-AI constructs and made novel contributions</p>
      <p>Suggested new directions of research for human automation research.</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <img src="/images/impact.png" alt="Impact" class="rounded-xl border w-full h-auto" />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
          I discovered three new relationships which better explain Human-AI Interaction contrary to theory.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    id="publication"
    class="scroll-mt-40 md:flex gap-x-10"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="publication-heading"
    tabindex="0"
  >
    <article class="md:w-[35%] space-y-6">
      <h2 id="publication-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Presentation</h2>
      <p>
        The culmination of my work was presented to key stakeholders, including the CEOs of 3PlayMedia and ScribeWire,
        representatives from broadcasters and providers (i.e Rogers) and advocacy groups
      </p>
      <p>Successfully defended at Toronto Metropolitan University</p>
    </article>
    <div class="md:w-[65%]">
      <figure>
        <iframe
          src="/docs/ai-captioning-presentation.pdf"
          class="w-full h-[360px] rounded-xl border"
          title="Thesis Defense"
        ></iframe>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Thesis presentation delivered to my defense committee.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</SectionedPageLayout>